{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>That your soul may bless me</b> — It was his intention to bless him that he should merit the blessing of Abraham, to inherit the land and to become the master of the covenant with Elohim, for he was the firstborn. And it appears that Rebecca never told him the prophecy that HaShem had spoken to her — \"and the elder shall serve the younger\" — for how could Isaac transgress the word of HaShem? But she would not succeed. Now at first she did not tell him, out of discipline and modesty, for \"she went to inquire of HaShem\" — she went without Isaac's permission. Or perhaps she said: I have no need to tell a prophecy to a prophet, for he is greater than the one who tells me. And now she did not wish to say to him: Thus was told to me from HaShem before I gave birth, for she said: because of his love for him he would not bless Jacob and would leave everything in the hands of Heaven. And she knew that through this cause Jacob would be blessed from his mouth with a whole heart and a willing soul. Or these are reasons from HaShem, so that Jacob would be blessed and Esau too with the blessing of the sword, and for Him alone the events were devised."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:35:41.323009669Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}